{"availability":"available","full":"BradyAJohnston/nodebpy","name":"nodebpy","description":"Build node trees in Blender more elegantly with code","category":"Developer tools","language":"Python","stars":118,"forks":6,"created":"2026-01-13T17:38:37Z","updated":"2026-10-08T16:36:11Z","license":"GPL-3.0","branch":"main","homepage":"https://bradyajohnston.github.io/nodebpy/","topics":["blender","blender-python","blender-scripts","geometry-nodes"],"demo":"https://bradyajohnston.github.io/nodebpy/","color":"#323057","ink":"#d6caff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T03:37:14.335Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-09T03:37:14.335Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-09T03:37:14.335Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-07T02:53:45.472Z","stars":113,"forks":6},{"at":"2026-10-09T03:37:14.335Z","stars":118,"forks":6}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Build node trees in Blender more elegantly with Python code. Geometry Nodes, Shader Nodes and Compositor nodes are all fully supported, with type hints and IDE auto-completion throughout.","A text-based version of nodes should bring the convenience of writing code with IDE auto-completion, type hinting, with overall compactness and readability, while staying as close as possible to what building a node tree via the GUI feels like."],"features":["Every node is a typed class named after the node it creates — 'Random Value' becomes g.RandomValue() — and node subtypes are class methods: g.RandomValue.vector().","Trees are built inside a with g.tree(...): context; instantiating a node class adds it to the current tree, and the tree's interface is declared with tree.inputs. / tree.outputs..","Nodes are linked with the >> operator, which picks the most compatible socket pair automatically (much like Node Wrangler's Alt + Right Click drag) — or address sockets explicitly through the .i. / .o. accessors.","Python's arithmetic, comparison and boolean operators create the matching Math / VectorMath / Compare / BooleanMath nodes: g.Value(1.0) 2 + (0, 0, 1).","Existing node trees — including ones wired up by hand in the GUI — can be exported back to nodebpy source with topython()."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/BradyAJohnston/nodebpy/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"ce11bfff89c4c8f4dc480ecdef6189058adc52b3d17494977762bb6317d009f3","extractedAt":"2026-10-09T03:37:14.478Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T03:37:14.478Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Build node trees in Blender more elegantly with Python code. Geometry Nodes, Shader Nodes and Compositor nodes are all fully supported, with type hints and IDE auto-completion throughout.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/BradyAJohnston/nodebpy/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"ce11bfff89c4c8f4dc480ecdef6189058adc52b3d17494977762bb6317d009f3","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/BradyAJohnston/nodebpy/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-09T03:37:14.478Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-10-08T16:36:11Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/BradyAJohnston/nodebpy/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-09T03:37:14.479Z","hash":"ce11bfff89c4c8f4dc480ecdef6189058adc52b3d17494977762bb6317d009f3","originalBytes":4403,"storedBytes":4403,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["node","nodes","nodebpy","python","trees","class","tree","code","g.randomvalue.vector","groups","api","arithmetic","auto-completion","back","boolean","classes","comparison","contributing.md","existing","g.cube","g.instanceonpoints","g.tree","geometry","gui","ide","inside","instance","like","math","methods","min","most","operators","pos","position","rot","sockets","tests","true","type","typed","writing","accessors","accessors.","add-on","adding","address","adds","after","alt","angle","anothertree","asset","auto-generated","automatically","bash","becomes","before","being","blender","blender-tracking","booleanmath","bradyajohnston.github.io","bring","broken","build","building","built","b